4.3 Answer Preselection
This is the task that motivated us first to explore Query Expansion techniques. We will use the WikiQA Dataset (Yang et al., 2015). The WikiQA corpus is an open set of question and sentence pairs, collected and annotated for research on open-domain question answering. For each question, we start a search on the set of answers with a similarity computation. We select the ten most similar answers, then we count the proportion of relevant answers in the ten hypotheses, taking into account that some questions have less than 10 possible answers. This will be our accuracy measure. Coverage is defined as the proportion of queries that had at least one appropriate answer among the ten hypotheses. We compare the accuracy measures using or not the Query Expansion engine. Here is an example of queries in the Dataset :
